# Supabase — Project Settings → API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Canonical public origin. Everything SEO-facing is built from this: canonical
# links, Open Graph URLs, the sitemap, JSON-LD and the RSS feed.
#
# Leave it unset. The default in src/lib/site.ts is https://amankrishna.in, and
# that default is deliberately NOT derived from VERCEL_URL — a preview
# deployment must never publish links to its own *.vercel.app host. Set this
# only if the site genuinely moves domains.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://amankrishna.in

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Fonts — powers the font picker in the article editor.
#
# Without it the picker falls back to the bundled font list; already-published
# articles keep rendering either way, because each article stores the families
# it uses. Create a key in Google Cloud console and enable "Web Fonts
# Developer API".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_FONTS_API_KEY=AIza...

# Origin the generated @font-face CSS is fetched from. Only change this if you
# self-host or proxy Google Fonts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FONT_CSS_ORIGIN=https://fonts.googleapis.com

# Note: GITHUB_TOKEN used to be listed here, but `src/lib/github.ts` sends no
# Authorization header — the live GitHub section uses the unauthenticated API
# and its own 1-hour cache. Setting the variable would have no effect, so it is
# not documented as an option.
